WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.100
My grandmother, like I said, my great-grandmother didn’t speak English.

2
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.800
They spoke Creole.

3
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.860
What they call Creole.

4
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:11.480
Creole French?

5
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.700
Yes.

6
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:18.180
The only thing is . . . We grew up with that.

7
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.000
But what they would tell us when we would go to school, “English!

8
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.220
No. When you go to school, you got to speak English.”

9
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:28.300
So we had to speak English in the schools, you know.

10
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:32.520
And we all went to Catholic school.

11
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:39.720
We stayed in our little neighborhoods, and that was it.

12
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.080
You grew up like that.

13
00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:48.800
My daddy used to say, “You see them children down there?

14
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:49.800
Don’t you play with them.

15
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.540
They’re too black.”

16
00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.420
They didn’t want you to mix.

17
00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.053
Of course it’s not like that now.

18
00:00:56.053 --> 00:00:58.700
You know, I mean, things have changed.

19
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:05.500
But at the height of segregation it was not nice.

20
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:16.260
That Jazz Fest made a big difference, because when you went to Jazz Fest, white, blacks, blue, greens, yellow, everybody’s out there having a good time.

21
00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:22.980
Nobody cared about nothing but the music and having a . . . Jazz Fest did something for New Orleans.

22
00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.400
It really did.

23
00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:29.060
Because people, like I said, they came from all over.

24
00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:36.540
And this is the only city [laughs] . . . You come out your house sometimes, and you hear music playing.

25
00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:39.680
They’re walking out in the street, they’re dancing.

26
00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:40.820
What are you doing?

27
00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:42.680
That’s a part of our culture.

28
00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:43.440
We love it.
